### Tailwind CSS Conventions

#### When to Check These Rules
- When adding or modifying styles
- When creating new components
- When working with custom Tailwind configurations

#### Rules
- Use TailwindCSS exclusively
- Document any custom classes in Tailwind config
- Avoid inline styles
- Follow Tailwind's utility-first approach
- Group related utilities with @apply when repeated
- Use consistent spacing and sizing scales
- Follow the mobile-first approach

#### Examples
✅ Correct:
```haml
.flex.items-center.gap-2
  .text-sm.font-medium.text-gray-700
    = label
```

✅ Correct Custom Class:
```css
/* tailwind.config.js */
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      gridTemplateColumns: {
        'service-provider': 'repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr))',
      }
    }
  }
}
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Using inline styles
- Not using utility classes
- Mixing utility and custom classes inconsistently
- Not following mobile-first approach

#### Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Using inline styles
- Not using utility classes
- Inconsistent spacing/sizing
- Not documenting custom classes
- Not following mobile-first approach

#### Validation Checklist
- [ ] Using Tailwind utility classes
- [ ] No inline styles
- [ ] Custom classes documented
- [ ] Consistent spacing/sizing
- [ ] Mobile-first approach
- [ ] Proper use of @apply
